# `make env` from the repo root turns this into a .env. Compose reads that .env
# from the project directory on its own, so nothing has to be exported in a shell
# or forwarded through the Makefile.
#
# .env is gitignored by bare name at any depth. This is a public repository:
# verify with `git check-ignore -v sites/house.bythewood.me/.env`.

# There is no password here. Signing in happens on auth.bythewood.me, and every
# route on this site asks that one whether the cookie in a request is live.

# Write-only ntfy token, minted by `make ntfy-token`. It pushes a notification
# when a new listing clears the filters and scores well, which is most of what
# this dashboard is worth: a dashboard only tells you when you open it. Unset
# means alerts are logged and never delivered, and a refresh still runs, because
# an alerter that cannot deliver must not stop the thing that noticed.
NTFY_TOKEN=

# RentCast, which is what makes this show real listings rather than whatever an
# agent last exported. Sign up at rentcast.io/api, the free plan is fifty
# requests a month, and one refresh spends one of them because a single request
# covers the whole search area.
#
# Unset means the adapter is skipped and the dashboard runs on the CSV imports
# alone. RentCast carries no photographs and no link to the original listing, so
# an agent's MLS export is still worth dropping in beside it.
RENTCAST_API_KEY=

# Reported crime, from the FBI Crime Data Explorer. The one fact on a report with
# no keyless route to it: the SBI publishes county crime as a PDF once a year and
# the FBI publishes it through an API that wants a key.
#
# The key is free and instant at api.data.gov/signup, with no card. Unset means the
# crime factor says it has no figures rather than guessing at one, and every other
# number on the page is unaffected.
FBI_API_KEY=
